Based on the logic of a NOT gate (inverter), the output is the logical negation of the input. In Verilog, this can be implemented using the `assign` statement with the bitwise NOT operator (`~`).

Here is the implementation:

```verilog
module TopModule (
  input in,
  output out
);

  assign out = ~in;

endmodule
```

